{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>And He charged Joshua.</b> The Holy One, blessed be He, charged him. And it refers to the beginning of the parashah." "<b>For you shall bring.</b> Since the children of Israel were not there, there was no need to accord them honor as above; therefore it says <b>for you shall bring the children of Israel.</b>"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {0 "Reading ואריש פר׳ קאי as ואת ראש פרשת קאי, 'and it refers to the beginning of the parashah,' understanding the vav of ואריש as 'and' prefixed to 'the beginning.'"}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:54:55.133843802Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}